cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "strategic-choice-anatomy: code and data for The internal anatomy of strategic choice in large language models"
message: "If you use this software or the released data, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vferraz/strategic-choice-anatomy"
abstract: >-
  Code, analysis and released data for a study of strategic behaviour and internal
  representations in large language models. Four models play all 144 Robinson-Goforth/Bruns
  canonical 2x2 games as one-shot natural-language decisions; the repository holds the
  collection runtime, the causal steering arm, and the layered behavioural, representational
  and token-attribution analyses that produce the paper's figures and tables.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - game theory
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - strategic decision making
  - activation steering
  - 2x2 games

authors:
